    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file that writes synthesized speech audio to a local file using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Polly service. Amazon Polly is a text-to-speech service that turns text into lifelike speech using deep learning. I will import the boto3 library to interact with Amazon Polly and use the synthesize_speech method to generate the audio. The provider will be identifiable by the import of boto3 and the use of the polly client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866397266,
          "start": 1789866395027
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
